WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.454
The OWASP Top 10 provides a practical recap of common application risks: broken access control, cryptographic failures, injection, insecure design, misconfiguration, vulnerable components, authentication failures, integrity failures, logging failures, and SSRF.

2
00:00:20.454 --> 00:00:38.114
CMMC practice domains help translate those risks into expectations for access control, audit and accountability, configuration management, identification and authentication, risk assessment, security assessment, system protection, and system integrity.

3
00:00:38.114 --> 00:00:52.382
Protecting CUI requires shared responsibility across software developers, DevSecOps teams, security engineers, IT administrators, defense contractors, compliance teams, and technical managers.

4
00:00:52.382 --> 00:00:55.306
Completion of this training is awareness-level only.

5
00:00:55.306 --> 00:01:01.791
It does not constitute certification, assessment completion, or proof of full organizational compliance.

6
00:01:01.791 --> 00:01:17.456
Useful follow-on materials include OWASP references, CMMC practice references, secure coding checklists, a glossary, an OWASP-to-CMMC mapping matrix, developer quick-reference sheets, and audit support documentation.

7
00:01:17.456 --> 00:01:19.960
Use this course as an awareness and planning aid.

8
00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.690
Validate practice applicability against the organization's CMMC scope.

9
00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:31.046
Maintain evidence for secure development, monitoring, configuration, and remediation activities.

10
